keel-overlay-etcd (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Monit's etcd-health check asks /health on etcd's plain metrics
    listener, http://[::1]:2381, which keel renders: the client port is
    TLS with client certificates now (keel's etcd over the mesh,
    handbook decision 0048), and a plain probe of it failed every cycle,
    so Monit restarted etcd forever.
  * The first installation marks /var/lib/etcd/default/member, in
    /var/lib/keel-overlay-etcd/package-member, when etcd-server's own
    postinst made it in the same transaction: a lone member of no
    cluster, which keel removes before it starts etcd for the mesh's
    cluster. A member that was there before is never marked, and keel
    refuses to start etcd over one it can not prove is the package's.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

keel-overlay-etcd (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041, first implementation, step 2).
    Depends on trixie's etcd-server 3.5.16 and on keel-overlay-wireguard,
    which the manifest requires; ships the overlay manifest of
    docs/manifest-v1.md as /usr/share/keel/overlays/etcd.yaml.
  * etcd.service is left disabled and stopped, the simple installation's
    state: postinst disables and stops it on the first installation only,
    after etcd-server's own postinst enabled and started it, and the
    preset 20-keel-overlay-etcd.preset keeps systemd's first boot preset
    from enabling it again. An upgrade of either package keeps whatever
    state keel apply has set since (packages/README.md).
  * postrm keeps the package in the config-files state after a remove, so
    a reinstall is an upgrade and leaves the unit alone; preinst records
    a unit already enabled or running before the first installation on a
    live system, never in an image build, and postinst leaves it as it
    was; postrm deletes that record on purge and abort-install.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
